    "body": "Yes, but at that point the incumbent will be whatever the global of the Realm of the MyCustomElement constructor is, assuming that constructor is not a built-in function.\r\n\r\nThe incumbent setup around calling into script is only needed when directly invoking built-in functions, basically.  Any time you've made it out into an actual scripted function, your incumbent is now the global of that function.",
